-- Configured finite atom/Unicode materialization count for the selected executable
-- generation (GH #813). This is NOT the mathematical capacity of Tier-0: the abstract
-- Tier-0 rank/address law is open-ended (n ∈ N). Never duplicate this generation count
-- as a SQL literal — the C binding reads LAPLACE_PERFCACHE_RECORD_COUNT from the
-- perfcache format header.
-- No DROP: atom_census() BEGIN ATOMIC depends on this; DROP would fail the
-- extension upgrade (GH #764). CREATE OR REPLACE is enough for the C binding.
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION laplace.atom_window()
    RETURNS bigint
    LANGUAGE C
    IMMUTABLE
    PARALLEL SAFE
    AS 'MODULE_PATHNAME', 'pg_laplace_atom_window';
